  "range_dependent": false,
  "finding": "The far block's apparently low look count is ENTIRELY the range profile inside it: detrending by the per-range-bin mean brings 210-246 from L=2.1 back to L=7.6, in line with every other block. CARRADA's speckle is uniform across range at ~7.5 looks and the range dependence lives in the MEAN, not in the look count. The generator therefore uses ONE look count and one mean profile, not a range-dependent look count.",
  "corollary": "The same mechanism inflates the far block's lag-1 correlations (range 0.75, Doppler 0.56 against 0.45 and 0.02 elsewhere): a shared range trend is common-mode across adjacent cells in both axes. It also inflates the FRAME-level lag-1 Doppler figure, so CARRADA's true Doppler speckle correlation is ~0.02-0.09, not 0.23."
